abstract: >-
  A reference asynchronous data-collection pipeline for OSINT use cases. Demonstrates
  aiohttp connection pooling, content-addressed deduplication via SHA-256, batched
  PostgreSQL writes with ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING, token-bucket rate limiting per
  source, and an optional Selenium WebDriver pool for JavaScript-rendered targets.
  Includes reproducible benchmarks measuring throughput improvements between sync
  and async strategies on three publicly-accessible APIs (NIST NVD, GitHub Events,
  OpenCorporates).
